      q: "The value of x such that x > 1, satisfying the equation ∫[1 to x] t ln t dt = 1/4 is",
      options: ["√e","e","e²","e - 1"],
      answer: 0,
      marks: 1,
      explanation: "1. WE NEED TO FIND x>1 SUCH THAT ∫[1 to x] t·ln(t) dt = 1/4. 2. FIRST, COMPUTE THE INDEFINITE INTEGRAL ∫t·ln(t) dt USING INTEGRATION BY PARTS: LET u=ln(t) (so du=(1/t)dt) AND dv=t dt (so v=t²/2). APPLYING THE FORMULA ∫u dv = uv − ∫v du: ∫t·ln(t) dt = (t²/2)·ln(t) − ∫(t²/2)·(1/t) dt = (t²/2)ln(t) − ∫(t/2) dt = (t²/2)ln(t) − t²/4 + C. 3. EVALUATE THE DEFINITE INTEGRAL FROM 1 TO x: [(x²/2)ln(x) − x²/4] − [(1²/2)ln(1) − 1²/4] = (x²/2)ln(x) − x²/4 − [0 − 1/4] (SINCE ln(1)=0) = (x²/2)ln(x) − x²/4 + 1/4. 4. SET THIS EQUAL TO 1/4 (GIVEN): (x²/2)ln(x) − x²/4 + 1/4 = 1/4. 5. SIMPLIFY BY SUBTRACTING 1/4 FROM BOTH SIDES: (x²/2)ln(x) − x²/4 = 0. 6. FACTOR OUT x²/4: x²/4 × [2ln(x) − 1] = 0. 7. SINCE x>1 (GIVEN), x²/4 ≠ 0, SO WE NEED 2ln(x) − 1 = 0, i.e., ln(x) = 1/2. 8. SOLVE FOR x: x = e^(1/2) = √e. 9. So THE VALUE OF x IS √e, matching option A."
