      answer: 4,
      tolerance: 0.01,
      kind: "nat",
      marks: 1,
      explanation: "1. INSERT THE VALUES 10,−4,15,30,20,5,60,19 IN ORDER INTO an INITIALLY EMPTY BINARY SEARCH TREE (BST), FOLLOWING STANDARD BST INSERTION RULES (SMALLER VALUES GO LEFT, LARGER VALUES GO RIGHT). 2. INSERT 10: BECOMES THE ROOT (TREE: {10}). 3. INSERT −4: SINCE −4<10, GOES TO THE LEFT OF 10 (TREE: 10 with LEFT CHILD −4). 4. INSERT 15: SINCE 15>10, GOES TO THE RIGHT OF 10 (TREE: 10 with LEFT=−4, RIGHT=15). 5. INSERT 30: SINCE 30>10, GO RIGHT to 15; SINCE 30>15, GOES TO THE RIGHT OF 15 (TREE: 15's RIGHT CHILD = 30). 6. INSERT 20: SINCE 20>10, GO RIGHT to 15; SINCE 20>15, GO RIGHT to 30; SINCE 20<30, GOES TO THE LEFT OF 30 (TREE: 30's LEFT CHILD = 20). 7. INSERT 5: SINCE 5<10, GO LEFT to −4; SINCE 5>−4, GOES TO THE RIGHT OF −4 (TREE: −4's RIGHT CHILD = 5) — THIS BRANCH DOESN'T AFFECT THE PATH TO 19. 8. INSERT 60: SINCE 60>10, GO RIGHT to 15; SINCE 60>15, GO RIGHT to 30; SINCE 60>30, GOES TO THE RIGHT OF 30 (TREE: 30's RIGHT CHILD = 60) — THIS BRANCH ALSO DOESN'T AFFECT THE PATH TO 19. 9. INSERT 19: SINCE 19>10, GO RIGHT to 15; SINCE 19>15, GO RIGHT to 30; SINCE 19<30, GO LEFT to 20; SINCE 19<20, GOES TO THE LEFT OF 20 (TREE: 20's LEFT CHILD = 19). 10. TRACE THE PATH FROM 19 UP TO THE ROOT: 19 → 20 → 30 → 15 → 10 — THIS PATH HAS 4 EDGES (19-20, 20-30, 30-15, 15-10). 11. So THE NUMBER OF EDGES IN THE PATH FROM 19 TO THE ROOT IS 4."
