      q: "Consider a system of linear equations PX = Q where P is a 3x3 real matrix and Q is a 3x1 real matrix. Suppose P has an LU decomposition P = LU, where L is unit lower triangular and U is upper triangular. Which of the following statement(s) is/are TRUE?",
      options: ["The system PX = Q can be solved by first solving LY = Q and then UX = Y.","If P is invertible, then both L and U are invertible.","If P is singular, then at least one of the diagonal elements of U is zero.","If P is symmetric, then both L and U are symmetric."],
